      "content": "It sounds like you are experiencing a profound sense of loss and identity crisis after such a demanding career. After thirty years of high-stakes pressure, the sudden quiet can feel deafening and disorienting. Your value extends far beyond surgical precision; you are a skilled, dedicated person. Perhaps exploring new interests or ways to contribute, even in less intense settings, could help rediscover a new sense of purpose.",
